2.8 Left and Right Shift Operators in C 
The left shift and right shift operators are << and >>. In left shift operations, the bits are shifted 
to the left and new locations are filled with zeros. On the other hand, for the right shift operation,

unsigned char a = 5, b = 9, c=255; 
unsigned char d= a << 2; //d = 00010100 --> decimal 20 
unsigned char e= b << 3; //e = 01001000 --> decimal 72 
unsigned char f= c << 2; //f = 11111100 --> decimal 252 
printf("d is %u", d); 
printf("\ne is %u", e); 
printf("\nf is %u", f); 
} 
